  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CE12112",
    "sub_id": "27400",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>1. Attendance: 5 %</div>\n\n<div>2.&nbsp;Homework: 12 %</div>\n\n<div>3.&nbsp;Quiz: 15 %</div>\n\n<div>4.&nbsp;Midterm exam: 30 %</div>\n\n<div>5.&nbsp;Final exam: 30 %</div>\n\n<div>6.&nbsp;Final project&nbsp;presentation: 8 %</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "Behavior in the classroom should always be timely, professional, well-prepared, and courteous. Effective learning can only be carried out if students, teachers, or other lecturers maintain mutual dignity and respect. In order to ensure a conducive learning environment, everyone is expected to do the following: abide by the classroom behavior rules and develop a polite culture.\n1. Students are expected to attend classes on time. If you cannot attend class on time, please do not select the course. Unless you are sick or have an emergency, you should arrive at the classroom on time and be seated before class starts. If you have to leave get out of class early for some reason, please let me know in advance.\n2. All students are expected to respect everyone in the classroom and to behave in a reasonable, responsible, and courteous manner at all times.\n3. Please do not talk, read, sleep, or do other non-course-related homework during class. Except for group discussions, side conversations should be kept to a minimum. If you are sitting next to someone who might chat with you during class, move to another seat so you don't give in to temptation.\n4. When your classmates are giving presentations or asking questions, you should listen attentively. When you present, you should face your group or the whole class and speak loudly so that your classmates can hear you.\n5. Laptops or tablets are allowed to be used for taking notes in class, otherwise, they should be put away.\n6. Make sure that mobile devices such as mobile phones and PDAs are turned off, put away, and kept in silent mode during class.\n7. Do not wear headphones in class.\n8. Dress neatly and avoid revealing clothing.",
    "course_pol_en": null,
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>Most courses have this declaration, also known as academic integrity. If you are interested in this course, then you must pay for the time and effort in exchange for the results. Ethics and honesty are the most important values. This means that illegal behavior (like cheating) is strictly prohibited and will be punished. So immerse yourself in this course and bring the best of yourself.</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": null,
    "ilearn_mk": null
  },
